  "findings": [
    "README,Win32entrypoint,resource/header/PCH and entire Data.cpp fully read. Project detects repeated game-item serial/type identities across character inventory and warehouses in SQL database,not file or image content duplicates. Inventory236/vault240fixed16byte item records; scans all flattened item pairs,skips special serials and shop exceptions. No byte-file hashing,pixel decoder or original-file confirmation.",
    "Matcher mutates in-memory item arrays while searching and optionally writes inventory/warehouse/account/character changes to DB. No original source snapshot,compare-before-update,transactional group receipt or completeness/error model. Count/fetch/read phases independent; repeated loop allocates new arrays without visible deletion,so unbounded repeated memory growth. No runtime/database/network or game execution performed; reject-domain now confirmed from core source.",
    "Seven item parser/helper files fully read. Item table16x512,IsItem checks ItemID>MAX_ITEMS rather than>= and omits negative check. OpenItemScript derives table pointer from parsed type/subtype before validating table bounds. This is source-level boundary review only; no malformed-input execution or production adoption.",
    "Tokenizer uses global FILE/token state,fixed1000byte token arrays without visible token-length guard,stores fgetc in char and returns partial quoted strings on EOF. Parser repeatedly consumes expected fields without checking token kind/EOF and copies name into32byte buffer. Thus no bounded validated parser contract to reuse. Object declarations are game/socket scaffolding; shared helper only updates Win32 title. No duplicate-file/image algorithm.",
    "Seven config/WinUtil/protocol/PCH/platform files fully read. Config loader ignores pConfig and writes global state; BanAccount reads BanCharacter key and vice versa. Minute-to-millisecond multiplication has no range validation. WinUtil/prodef are game packet headers and byte operations,not content fingerprints. No protocol/network/game execution.",
    "PCH defines MAX_TYPE_PLAYER5 while already-read ReadItems writes RequireClass[CLASS_SUMMONER5] and[CLASS_RAGEFIGHTER6], beyond five-element array. Protection SDK inclusion conditional defaults disabled; no vendor protection modification or execution. Platform macros target legacy Windows. These are source-derived rejection reasons,not runtime qualification or adopted code.",
    "ODBC query and log modules fully read. Binary read API accepts no destination capacity and returns last chunk length rather than total; caller ignores return. Pointer advance accumulates offsets repeatedly across chunks. Non-success reads not cleanly separated from valid data; fixed caller buffers/record lengths lack returned-size validation. SetAsBinary returns void without checked commit receipt; no transaction or compare-before-update guard.",
    "Query lock ownership is tracked by shared bool and next ExecQuery may Close prior cursor; no per-operation RAII or caller-thread ownership model. Error paths leave cleanup to external Close. Logs format into fixed buffers with unchecked formatting; LogTextAdd writes len+1 even at maximum row length, and UI reads global ring without consistent lock. No runtime,DB or malformed-input execution; these source patterns are not adopted."
  ],
